{"term":"prototype","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:f24bbfa0d19ebcf92b","definition":"An original form or object which is a basis for other forms or objects (particularly manufactured items), or for its generalizations and models.","example":"Near-synonym: archetype (sometimes synonymous)","pos":"noun","synonyms":["archetype","exemplar"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["pretotype","prototypable","prototypal","prototype-based","prototype-based language","prototype-based programming","prototype-based scripting language","prototype extension","prototype-oriented","prototype-oriented programming","prototype pattern","prototype theory","prototypic","prototypical","prototypicality","prototypically","prototyping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prototype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c0c7de4c8b661319d1","definition":"An early sample or model built to test a concept or process.","example":"The prototype had loose wires and rough edges, but it worked.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["pretotype","prototypable","prototypal","prototype-based","prototype-based language","prototype-based programming","prototype-based scripting language","prototype extension","prototype-oriented","prototype-oriented programming","prototype pattern","prototype theory","prototypic","prototypical","prototypicality","prototypically","prototyping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prototype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:80f94a84331bd5f5e3","definition":"A declaration of a function that specifies the name, return type, and parameters, but none of the body or actual code.","example":"Like any variable in a C program it is necessary to prototype or declare a function before its use, if it returns a value other than an int. It informs the compiler that the function would be referenced at a later stage in the program. / For example, / In program 1, the statement / void display_message(); / is a function prototype or declaration. Here void specifies that this function does not return any value, and the empty parenthesis^([sic – meaning parentheses]) indicate that it takes no parameters (arguments).","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["pretotype","prototypable","prototypal","prototype-based","prototype-based language","prototype-based programming","prototype-based scripting language","prototype extension","prototype-oriented","prototype-oriented programming","prototype pattern","prototype theory","prototypic","prototypical","prototypicality","prototypically","prototyping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prototype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2bdabb67f331b008c2","definition":"An instance of a category or a concept that combines its most representative attributes.","example":"A robin is a prototype of a bird; a penguin is not.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["pretotype","prototypable","prototypal","prototype-based","prototype-based language","prototype-based programming","prototype-based scripting language","prototype extension","prototype-oriented","prototype-oriented programming","prototype pattern","prototype theory","prototypic","prototypical","prototypicality","prototypically","prototyping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prototype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:38a36f43d20d15c413","definition":"A type of race car, a racing sports car not based on a production car. A 4-wheeled cockpit-seating car built especially for racing on sports car circuits, that does not use the silhouette related to a consumer road car.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["racing prototype","sports prototype","prototype racecar"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["pretotype","prototypable","prototypal","prototype-based","prototype-based language","prototype-based programming","prototype-based scripting language","prototype extension","prototype-oriented","prototype-oriented programming","prototype pattern","prototype theory","prototypic","prototypical","prototypicality","prototypically","prototyping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prototype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5e03d0ad5c09c29208","definition":"To create a prototype of.","example":"In short, he has purposely perverted the whole case from beginning to end, and distorted it in such a manner, as not to be prototyped except by his own mind; […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["pretotype","prototypable","prototypal","prototype-based","prototype-based language","prototype-based programming","prototype-based scripting language","prototype extension","prototype-oriented","prototype-oriented programming","prototype pattern","prototype theory","prototypic","prototypical","prototypicality","prototypically","prototyping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prototype#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:39f88dc41f59ef5719","definition":"To imitate or emulate.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"rare","register":"rare, transitive","wordFamily":["pretotype","prototypable","prototypal","prototype-based"